course: dictionary
lesson: 1570
title: One word, many meanings: charge
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «charge» has several meanings. Read the words around it, and they will tell you which one is right. «The shop will charge £3 for delivery» is about money. A charge is the price you pay, so the words around it give you the clue.
explain: «My phone needs charging before the trip.» Here charge means to fill a battery with electric power. «The bull began to charge across the field» is different: it means to run hard and fast straight at something. Ask yourself, "What fits here?" then test your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Charge can also mean to lead and decide. «Ella is in charge of the class while the teacher is away» means Ella is the one who leads. Charge can even mean to say officially that someone did a crime. Always check the words around the word, then try your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Charge is a verb and a noun: you can charge a phone, or pay a charge.
fact: «Free of charge» means it costs nothing.
fact: «Overcharged» means asked for more money than the right price.
fact: Electricity is a flow of tiny charged particles through a material.
fact: Do not put a phone in a microwave: it can catch fire. Ollie's TikTok idea is a myth, not a way to charge.
exercise: «My phone needs charging before the trip.» What does charging mean here? | *Filling it with electric power | Telling the police about it | Running hard straight at it | Asking money for it
exercise: «The bull began to charge across the field.» What does charge mean? | Lead and decide | Ask a price | *Run hard straight at something | Fill with power
exercise: «Ella is in charge of the class while the teacher is away.» What does in charge mean? | Has the battery for the class | Is very angry with the class | Asks money from the class | *Leads and decides for the class
test: «Free of charge» means what? | It costs a lot | *It costs nothing | It runs very fast | It is a crime
test: Ollie says a phone charges if you put it in a microwave. What is true? | *Microwaves are not for phones, and the idea is a myth | It works if the phone is cold | Phones are charged by the sun | Microwaves charge phones in ten seconds
exam: «Being charged too much is called being overcharged.» What does overcharged mean? | Given a free gift | Lost in the shop | *Asked for more money than the right price | Charged the right price
